# The last pool, and a victory lap by design.
#
# Every rule the game has is on this board - a refusing arrow, an arrow to aim
# down, a corridor that only fills backwards, a cross serving three ways, two
# thirsts that each cost a dead-end branch - but most of the plumbing is already
# laid. The board is the biggest in the game and the par is not: 13 against
# level 23's 15, so difficulty peaks at 23 and this one sends the player off.
#
# It was par 20 in its first cut, which made it the hardest level in the game.
# Ending a cozy puzzle on its hardest board is exactly the feeling Pillar 1
# exists to prevent, so I pre-laid four tiles rather than shrink the pool.
id: 24
